A continuous function is computable when membership in its graph is r.e. The constant finite sets are the first case.

**Theorem (`mem_graph_const_iff`).** $m$ lies in the graph of the constant function with value $e_n$ if and only if $m$ is a code for a pair $(a, b)$ and the bit of $n$ at position $b$ is on. Equivalently, $b \in e_n$.
